<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Valentín Gómez Farías</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1781–1858</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Valentín Gómez Farías was a Mexican physician and liberal politician who served as vice-president and acting president several times in the 1830s and 1840s. In 1833–1834, while Santa Anna stayed away from the capital, he launched reforms that ended compulsory church tithes, cut the privileges of the clergy and army, and secularised education. Santa Anna reversed the reforms in 1834, and Gómez Farías went into exile.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/valentin-gomez-farias.jpg" alt="Valentín Gómez Farías" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: José Inés Tovilla · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Valent%C3%ADn_G%C3%B3mez_Far%C3%ADas,_portrait.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
